INT. SURPRISE PARTY - APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - DARK - EVENING

Balloons. A banner. A cake with too many candles. Five adults crouch behind furniture, whispering, trying not to giggle.

BEATRIX "BEA" LINDQVIST-ADE, 40s, behind the couch with a noisemaker. COLM FITZGIBBON, 30s, behind the armchair holding a camera. ROSALIND "ROZ" PELLEGRINO-OKON, 50s, under the dining table with the cake. YOSHIRO BAPTISTE, 20s, crouched by the door, finger on the lights. And TIBERIUS "TIBBY" MORROW, 60s, hidden inside the coat closet.

BEA
(whispering)
She's coming up the stairs.

COLM
(whispering)
How do you know?

BEA
I hear her keys.

ROZ
She's got the wrong keys.

YOSHIRO
Shh!

The doorknob rattles. All five freeze. A key scrapes and fails. Another. A third.

TIBBY
(from the closet)
Is it her?

BEA
Quiet!

The door swings open. A silhouette in the hall: a stranger in a delivery uniform, holding a pizza box.

DELIVERY GUY
Uh. Hello?

Yoshiro flips the lights. Everyone leaps up.

ALL
Surprise!

Roz pitches the cake into the air. Colm's flash goes off. Bea blows the noisemaker in the Delivery Guy's face. He yelps, the pizza flies, the cake lands on Tibby as he tumbles out of the closet.

Silence. Frosting drips from Tibby's nose. The Delivery Guy stares at them all.

DELIVERY GUY (CONT'D)
...Does anyone here order a large pepperoni?

BEA
(weakly)
Wrong apartment?

DELIVERY GUY
Apparently.

Tibby licks frosting from his lip.

TIBBY
Well. I'll take the pizza.
